id: feint
name: Feint
type: instant
actionCost: 0
kiCostPerTier: 2
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
clashSkill: bluff
clashDefenderSkills: intuition, perception
feint: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Sell the wrong move. A Clash of your Bluff against their Intuition or Perception, and
  winning buys a Basic Attack out of sequence at 1(T) better and almost undefendable -
  with no Area of Effect and a quarter of your Capacity as the most you may wager.
text: >
  Feint Maneuver [1/Round]: Draw your opponent’s attention away from your true
  intentions before you strike!
  –Maneuver Type: Instant Maneuver
  –Action Cost: N/A
  –Minions: N/A
  –KP Cost: 2(T)
  –Effect: Target an Opponent within your Melee Range. Make a Clash (Bluff vs
  Intuition/Perception) against that Opponent. If you win, you may use the Basic Attack
  Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver. Increase the Strike and Wound Rolls for this
  Attacking Maneuver by 1(T) and your Opponent cannot use any option of the Defend
  Maneuver in response to this Attacking Maneuver except Cross Counter, but this
  Attacking Maneuver cannot possess an AoE and you cannot Ki Wager more than 1/4
  (rounded up) of your Maximum Capacity on this Attacking Maneuver.

---

# --- The Clash ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "(Bluff vs Intuition/Perception)". The slash is a choice made by whoever is rolling -
# the same slash as in "Strike/Dodge" and "(Impulsive/Corporeal)", both of which are read
# that way - so the defender is asked which of the two before either side sees a number.
#
# A tie goes to the Defender, here as everywhere: a feint has to be sold outright.
#
# --- What winning buys ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "You may use the Basic Attack Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver", which is the
# Exploit Maneuver's shape and reaches the same door - an offer on the card, taken by the
# player, waiving the Action Cost and nothing else.
#
# What is new is that the attack arrives with conditions attached. Four of them, two for
# and two against, and they travel with the offer rather than being remembered anywhere:
#
#   - +1(T) on the Strike Roll and on the Wound Roll, as a row each on the breakdown
#   - no option of the Defend Maneuver but Cross Counter
#   - no Area of Effect
#   - a Ki Wager of at most 1/4 of your Maximum Capacity, rounded up
#
# The two against are refused where the attack is declared rather than checked after it:
# a Profile with an Area is offered greyed out with the reason on it, and the wager field's
# ceiling comes down. Being told afterwards that the attack you built is illegal is worse
# than not being able to build it.
#
# "1/4 of your MAXIMUM Capacity", not what is left of it - so it is a ceiling on this
# attack and not a second reading of what you can afford. The ordinary limits still apply
# underneath: you cannot wager Capacity you have spent or Ki you have not got.
#
# Rounded up, which is unusual here and is what the entry says.
#
# --- Melee Range -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Target an Opponent within your Melee Range." Said and not policed, like every other
# range in this system: nothing here measures a distance. The attack it buys is a Basic
# Attack and carries its own reach rules, which are policed where every attack's are.
#
# --- Instant ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The first Special Maneuver that is not a Standard one. Being an Instant brings the rule
# with it: not two in a row, and only in answer to a Standard Maneuver - both of which live
# in `whyNotAnotherInstant` and the respond machinery already, and neither needed anything
# here.
#
# Worth noticing: the Out-of-Sequence Basic Attack this hands over does not count as a
# Maneuver in the Instant's place, which is what the Out-of-Sequence door has always said.
#
# --- How it is gained ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Bluff, at the 2+ Ranks every Skill grants a Special Maneuver at: "Special Maneuver: you
# gain access to the Feint Maneuver" is in the Skill's own entry, which is the only place
# that ever says so.
#
# Worth saying, because it looked otherwise: the Dirty Trick Maneuver is also a Clash made
# with Bluff and is NOT opened by it. Being the Skill a Maneuver rolls and being the Skill
# that hands it over are two different questions, and only the Skill's entry answers the
# second.
